course: dictionary
lesson: 6673
title: A name with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Oberon is a name, and names begin with a capital letter. Sometimes one name has more than one meaning, so context helps you choose the right one. Read the sentence: «Uranus's moons are named after characters from Shakespeare and Alexander Pope, such as Miranda, Titania and Oberon.»
explain: The clues are «moons» and «named after characters». These tell you that Oberon here is a moon, not a person you know. The word «Uranus» tells you which planet the moon belongs to.
explain: Oberon can also be the name of a character in old stories. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence you are reading. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Oberon is a name, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: In old European folklore and stories, «Oberon» is the king of the fairies.
fact: In famous plays, Oberon is the fairy king and the husband of Titania.
fact: «Oberon» is also the second-largest moon of the planet Uranus.
fact: Oberon was discovered by William Herschel in 1787. It is a cold, icy moon covered in craters.
exercise: In «Uranus's moons are named after characters from Shakespeare and Alexander Pope, such as Miranda, Titania and Oberon.», what is Oberon? | *A moon of Uranus | A kind of planet with rings | A famous poet | A wizard's spell
exercise: Who is Oberon in old stories and plays? | A giant who lives on a hill | A talking horse | *The king of the fairies | The queen of the sea
exercise: Who discovered Oberon? | *William Herschel | Shakespeare | Alexander Pope
test: Oberon is the second-largest moon of which planet? | Saturn | Neptune | Mercury | *Uranus
test: What kind of word is Oberon? | *A name | A verb | A number | An adjective
exam: Which best describes Oberon in «Uranus's moons are named after characters from Shakespeare and Alexander Pope, such as Miranda, Titania and Oberon.»? | A type of rock | A sea creature | A kind of weather | *A moon of Uranus, named after a character from a story
